<title>GERMANY: Linde won't redenominate shares until EMU.</title>
<headline>Linde won't redenominate shares until EMU.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>German engineering group Linde AG said on Tuesday it would wait for the start of European currency union, slated to begin in January 1999, before redenominating its shares.</p>
<p>Linde shares have a nominal value of 50 marks.</p>
<p>&quot;When the euro comes, Linde will redenominate its shares,&quot; Linde chief executive Hans Meinhardt said in response to a question at the group's annual general meeting.</p>
<p>Many publicly-listed German companies have redenominated their shares to a nominal value of five marks.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
